Ascended a Wizard on my office computer.

It's a game that I was tempted to quit, since I didn't mean to start
a Wizard and this one had really crummy starting stats and nothing
in the starting equipment to speak of.  Basically this Wizard started
her mission as a wimpy "fighter-mage", and did the protection racket.

It was touch-and-go quite a few times getting to minetown, as it
always is in these games.  At least five separate fights got her
to one HP, but she made it, and minetown was coaligned.  At this
point, I started to get interested in the game.  There was nothing
really memorable in minetown.  I think the most interesting thing
was a tinning kit, seriously, a very few un-id scrolls (not ID),
and some food.

Itzchak didn't have anything but candles.  So anyway, the game was
pretty long and boring after that.  Sokoban provided a BoH.  She
found plenty of spellbooks but the first read of most spells timed
out long before she could ditch her armor, so she rarely did any
spellcasting in the first 50K turns.  I played her like a ranger
-- an Elf with a stack of +7 elven daggers at expert is pretty good
anyway.  Did the castle without getting levitation first, which was
quite the gambit.  Did the gears and tumblers method of opening the
castle.  There were lev boots in the castle.  This was the first
time any of my characters has killed Medusa without stoning her,
and she got tinned and taken to the planes.  It was also my first
game ever where Rodney left a corpse, so he's canned as well.

After that, the game got pretty boring.  She was altar camping and a
random black pudding was dumb enough to show up at her altar, so I
went ahead and took up the RNG's offer, plenty of spellbooks and
an accidental crowning - oh well.

At some point, I guess some pet of hers killed Itzchack, but I don't
know how or who or when.

At the endgame she didn't bother with anything more than getting
her AK together.  Made sure to get the scrolls of gold detection,
organize the pack, and get unburdened as possible.  Plane of Water
was terribly frustrating, and an attempt at genociding sea monsters
resulted in a typo and wiped out leprechauns instead.  Until then,
the only thing that had been genocided was mimics, which paid off
nicely in random shops and in Orcustown.

Pestilence made a beeline for my character and her posse, and got
at least 3 illness attacks in.  Wrong altar.  Death didn't even get
in the way, but also wrong altar.

Famine had the Chaotic altar, and Wyvern the Wizard wished up a
Ki-Rin (named Coffee) and a blessed fireproof saddle, to ride from
the Astral Plane in style.  A Xorn (named Hungry) and a
Titanothere (named Butts) tagged along.  There were a LOT of pets
this game, since my character had Charm Monster and Polymorph at
0% fail for so much of the game.  I don't know why the Jabberwock (named 
Lutwidge), the Owlbear (named Huggy), or the Gray Dragon (named Puff)
didn't come along.


